hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19265","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from Thabit al-Bunani from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Abu Layla who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in a prayer that was not obligatory. He passed by mention of Paradise and the Fire and said: I seek refuge in Allah from the Fire; woe to the people of the Fire."
"19266","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from his brother Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from his grandfather who said: We were at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Hasan ibn Ali came crawling until he climbed upon his chest and urinated on him. We rushed to take him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My son, my son. Then he called for water and poured it over it."
"19267","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Isa from Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Abu Layla that he was at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with al-Hasan or al-Husayn on his belly, Zuhayr doubted. He urinated until I saw his urine in streams upon the belly of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We rushed to him. He said, upon him be prayer and peace: Leave my son, do not frighten my son. Then he called for water and poured it over it. He took a date from the charity dates and put it in his mouth. The Messenger of Allah took it out of his mouth."
"19268","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah from Qays ibn Muslim from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from his father who said: I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the conquest of Khaybar. When they fled we fell upon their baggage. People took what they found of household goods. No sooner had the pots boiled than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the pots overturned, and divided among us, making for every ten a sheep."
"19269","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Isa from his father from his grandfather from Abu Layla who said: I was at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with al-Hasan or al-Husayn on his chest or belly. I saw his urine in streams. We went to him. He said: Leave my son, do not frighten him until he finishes his urine. Then he followed it with water. Then he stood and entered the charity dates house, the boy entering with him. He took a date and put it in his mouth. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extracted it and said: Charity is not lawful for us."
"19270","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us from Ibn Abi Layla from Thabit who said: I was sitting with Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla in the mosque. A bulky man was brought and said: O Abu Isa. He said: Yes. He said: Narrate to us what you heard about fur. He said: I heard my father say: I was sitting at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, may I pray in fur? He said: Where is tanning? When he turned I said: Who is this? He said: This is Suwayd ibn Ghafalah."
"19271","Abdullah narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ali ibn Abis narrated to us from Abu Fazarah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from his father, as far as I know, Musa doubted, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed itikaf in a dome of palm leaves."
"19272","Harun ibn Maruf, Abu Mamar, and Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Samti narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us from Abu Fazarah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observe itikaf in a dome of palm leaves."
